//~ CHECK-ONLY
// prims (sequential): the bulk operations stage1 passes call instead of writing their own loops.
//
// Modules:
//   word      the unsigned integer types the generic operations accept
//   col       constructors of filled columns
//   xxhash    xxHash32
//   sort      stable LSD radix `sort_perm` of u8 / u16 / u32 / u64 keys
//   scan      exclusive / inclusive prefix sums, offsets
//   select    stream compaction by flags
//   rle       run-length encoding
//   search    lower_bound / upper_bound over a sorted column
//   perm      gather, scatter, inverse permutation
//   bracket   matching partner of each bracket of a depth-coded column
//   bits      rows of bits
//   ragged    offsets + data, rows as slices
//   hindex    lookup-only hash index
//
// Every result depends on the input values alone, never on the order the elements are visited in
// (stable sorts, duplicate indices resolved by position), so a data-parallel implementation gives
// the same bytes. Sizes and positions are `usize`; ids and offsets stored in columns are `u32`
// (a length above `u32::MAX` traps `Assert`).
